   "he": "שְׁבוּעַת הָעֵדוּת — דִּכְתִיב: ״וְנֶפֶשׁ כִּי תֶחֱטָא וְשָׁמְעָה קוֹל אָלָה״ — בְּכׇל לָשׁוֹן שֶׁהִיא שׁוֹמַעַת.",
   "en": "It is stated in the mishna that «an oath of testimony» may be said in any language, «as it is written: “And if anyone sins, in that he heard the voice of adjuration”» (Leviticus 5:1). The emphasis on hearing in the verse is interpreted to mean that it can be recited «in any language that a person hears,» i.e., understands."
  }
